NUM-23: scale transect bank stations exactly like the stations

setParams() in transect.c scaled the overbank stations as
(x/UCF(LENGTH))*Xfactor while addStation() scales every station as
x*Xfactor/UCF(LENGTH). getFlow() finds the banks by exact equality (Station[k]
== Xleftbank), so in SI units with a width factor the two roundings often
differ by one ulp, no bank is found and the whole section is computed as one
subsection with the right overbank's n. Compute the banks with the same
expression as the stations. US units and SI without a width factor give
bit-identical values to before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-23_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
index c8e58ca..9af3cca 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
@@ -377,8 +377,8 @@ int  setParams(int j, char* id, double x[])
     if ( Lfactor == 0.0 ) Lfactor = 1.0;
     Xfactor = x[8];                              // station location multiplier
     if ( Xfactor == 0.0 ) Xfactor = 1.0;
-    Xleftbank *= Xfactor;                        // adjusted left bank
-    Xrightbank *= Xfactor;                       // adjusted right bank
+    Xleftbank = x[3] * Xfactor / UCF(LENGTH);    // adjusted left bank
+    Xrightbank = x[4] * Xfactor / UCF(LENGTH);   // adjusted right bank
     Yfactor = x[9] / UCF(LENGTH);                // elevation offset
     Nstations = 0;
     return 0;
